/T (5. Cryptanalysis and Security Vulnerability Assessment While simple to implement, the student organization's reliance on a fixed shift cipher represents a critical vulnerability in network security architecture. This cipher is acutely susceptible to two primary forms of cryptanalysis: Brute Force \(Exhaustive Key Search\): The key space size of a standard shift cipher is exceptionally small. Because the English alphabet contains only 26 characters, there are exactly 26 - 1 = 25 possible unique keys \(a shift of 0 or 26 returns the original text completely unmodified\). An adversary capturing "QIIX EX RSSR" can execute a complete exhaustive search in milliseconds manually, or microseconds)
