/T (To detect this, forensic investigators apply LSB visual filtration. Tools like StegExpose or custom Python scripts strip away the most significant bits \(which carry the core visual structure of the logo\) and isolate only the least significant bits. If the image is clean, the isolated LSB layer looks like natural, unstructured random noise. If the logo contains hidden data, the LSB filtration reveals distinctive blocks or high- contrast structural patches where data was sequentially injected, exposing a non-random distribution of structural binary data.)
/E (To detect this, forensic investigators apply LSB visual filtration. Tools like StegExpose or custom Python scripts strip away the most significant bits \(which carry the core visual structure of the logo\) and isolate only the least significant bits. If the image is clean, the isolated LSB layer looks like natural, unstructured random noise. If the logo contains hidden data, the LSB filtration reveals distinctive blocks or high- contrast structural patches where data was sequentially injected, exposing a non-random distribution of structural binary data.)
