/T (Methodology C: File Structure and Metadata Integrity Inspection: Many rudimentary data-hiding applications do not inject data directly into the pixel configurations; instead, they append payloads to the file's structural boundaries. Every file format has designated hex markers establishing its boundary rules. A standard PNG file must initiate with the hex header sequence 89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A and conclude with the End-of-Image trailer marker 49 45 4E 44 AE 42 60 82. A standard JPEG starts with FF D8 and terminates with FF D9.)
/E (Methodology C: File Structure and Metadata Integrity Inspection: Many rudimentary data-hiding applications do not inject data directly into the pixel configurations; instead, they append payloads to the file's structural boundaries. Every file format has designated hex markers establishing its boundary rules. A standard PNG file must initiate with the hex header sequence 89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A and conclude with the End-of-Image trailer marker 49 45 4E 44 AE 42 60 82. A standard JPEG starts with FF D8 and terminates with FF D9.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
