/T (Before embedding, the data payload is encrypted using a modern symmetric standard, such as Advanced Encryption Standard \(AES\) with a 256-bit key operating in Galois/Counter Mode \(GCM\). This ensures that even if a forensic investigator discovers and extracts the data layer, it appears as absolute cryptographic noise. Without the private AES key, it cannot be decrypted. The encrypted text is then passed through a compression algorithm \(like DEFLATE\). Compression strips away structural repetitions and patterns, maximizing the data's entropy. This makes it much harder for statistical steganalysis tools \(like the Chi-Square test\) to differentiate between the hidden data and normal pixel noise.)
/E (Before embedding, the data payload is encrypted using a modern symmetric standard, such as Advanced Encryption Standard \(AES\) with a 256-bit key operating in Galois/Counter Mode \(GCM\). This ensures that even if a forensic investigator discovers and extracts the data layer, it appears as absolute cryptographic noise. Without the private AES key, it cannot be decrypted. The encrypted text is then passed through a compression algorithm \(like DEFLATE\). Compression strips away structural repetitions and patterns, maximizing the data's entropy. This makes it much harder for statistical steganalysis tools \(like the Chi-Square test\) to differentiate between the hidden data and normal pixel noise.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
