<<
/Title (2. Forensic Detection Methodologies \(Steganalysis\) When digital investigators suspect that a corporate logo or media asset contains a hidden data cache, they apply the science of steganalysis. Because modern data hiding algorithms minimize visual degradation, detection relies on metadata auditing, spatial domain manipulation, and statistical anomalies. Methodology A: Statistical Cryptanalysis and Color Histogram Deviation Analysis: Digital images store color values within complex pixel matrices. For example, in a standard 24-bit TrueColor image, each individual pixel contains three bytes representing the intensity channels for Red, Green, and Blue \(RGB\), yielding values between 0 and 255 per channel. When data hiding occurs, the specific values of these channels are altered systematically.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 944 0 R
>>
endobj
