/Title (Methodology B: Spatial Consistency Auditing and Least Significant Bit \(LSB\) Visual Filtering: The most ubiquitous approach to hiding data in images is LSB modification. This technique strips the lowest- order bit of a pixel's color byte and replaces it with a bit from the hidden payload. Because changing the last bit changes the color value by only 1 unit \(e.g., from an RGB value of 140 to 141\), the visual difference is completely imperceptible to the human eye.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 950 0 R
/Next 956 0 R
>>
endobj
